[
  {
    "text": "THE STUDENTS' POCKET PRESCRIBES.- ?t?y \r\nCHI\u0002Dr. D. M. Macdonald, M.D., F.R.C.P.E. 9th Edi\u0002tion. Edinburgh; E. & D. Livingstone, 1925. \r\nPp. 226. Price, 3s. net. \r\nIn a miniature volume which will readily go into \r\nthe vest pocket, the author has condensed no less than \r\n551 prescriptions with directions for use. They are \r\narranged according to the diseases for which they \r\nare intended. \r\nThere is a great deal of information on prescribing, \r\na table of doses, a vocabulary, diet tables, etc. This \r\nhandy and cheap volume will be found very useful \r\nby students and doctors. It has reached the 9th edi\u0002tion and is becoming increasingly popular. \n",
